DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 2

Bash Scripting Basics (0–2 Years Experience)

If you want to grow in DevOps, manual work is your enemy.
Bash scripting helps you automate tasks, reduce errors, and save time — and interviewers love this skill.

📌 Tools 2 Focus: Bash Scripting – Interview Questions

• What is Bash scripting and why is it used in DevOps?
• Difference between shell and bash
• What is a shebang (#!/bin/bash)?
• How do you create and run a shell script?
• What are variables in bash?
• Difference between local and environment variables
• How do you take user input in a script?
• What are positional parameters ($1, $2, $@, $#)?
• Difference between $@ and $*
• What is exit status in bash?
• What does $? represent?
• Conditional statements (if, elif, else)
• Loop types in bash (for, while)
• Difference between while and until loop
• How do you write comments in bash?
• How do you make a script executable?
• What is set -x and set -e?
• How do you redirect output (>, >>, 2>)
• What is piping (|) and why is it important?
• Simple real-world example of a bash script

💡 Interview Tip:
If you explain a script like:

👉 “I wrote a bash script to clean logs, monitor disk usage, or automate backups”
—you instantly look like a practical DevOps engineer, not a fresher.
